Last Week in Marugame

News is out; I am being transferred to a place called Sennan in Wakayama
Zone (Sennan is technically in Osaka Prefecture but that's a nitpicky
detail)
I am going to be companions with one of my district member=E2=80=99s past
companions, Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81. He is from the Phillipines, and a cr=
azy character to
say the least. Very interested to see how we will work as a companionship!
It's odd to go into a new companionship already knowing a bit about my
companion. Hopefully that will be a good thing haha.

Tuesday this week we had DCM, the last one in this District for me. We went
all the way to Toyo to have it in person with the District Leader
companionship. It was around 2 hours travel there, and it cost a decent
amount too. We ended up having to cut it short because of the other Elders
having a lesson appointment, but we talked a lot about inviting friends to
baptism. The sister missionaries have invited 3 friends to baptism and all
of them said yes and have dates planned! One of their baptisms will be next
week! Too bad I won't be there =F0=9F=98=A2 On our way home from Toyo we mi=
ssed a
train, and the total travel was around 4-5 hours. Not to mention, when we
got back to the station in Marugame my bike and one of the Sister
Missionary=E2=80=99s bikes had been stolen =F0=9F=98=B6 We went to the poli=
ce and let them
know, and walked all the way back to our apartments. Bummmmmerrrrr (the
story isn=E2=80=99t over????)

Wednesday-Friday
I am writing this all pretty late so I don=E2=80=99t remember a lot of deta=
ils, but
a few notable things happened. The sister missionaries in our area=E2=80=99=
s
neighbor was a huge help to us this week. After my bike was stolen, they
found out and let us borrow their Son=E2=80=99s bike for the foreseeable fu=
ture. He
rode it all the way over to the apartment, and his parents drove away and
left him to walk home lol. They are an interesting family for sure.
Fortunately, we found out that our bikes hadn=E2=80=99t been stolen but rat=
her
confiscated by a rental bike company for being in front of the station for
longer than they should have been. Not sure if that is legal but ok. I had
to pay about 10 bucks fee but I was just happy to have the bike back. The
bike that the friend dropped off at our apartment ironically never got
used, we were actually able to get back my bike the day after it went
missing. The same people that dropped off that bike also helped me to get
my suitcases to the train station so that I didn=E2=80=99t have to walk all=
 the way
there, was a lifesaver. Unnnnnfortunately we went to have a =E2=80=9Clast s=
upper=E2=80=9D
with Nakamura=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F in our ward. We went with Tatsuya!

It was great, and I think that they get along really well. There was a
video of a Japanese restaurant (opening in India I think) playing on the
tablet that we used to order our food. I said in Japanese that it was a
bunch of foreigners, and for some reason Tatsuya thought it was super funny
and started choking on his water for a minute there lol. I was trying to
play it off casually but I was snickering a little bit too haha. After our
dinner, we got back to finish packing before the Sister=E2=80=99s neighbor =
arrived.
Unfortunately I had a lot of stuff to pack last minute and took like 10
minutes longer than She had expected, and we were half yelled at in the car
all the way to the station about being late and how unacceptable that is in
Japan. It is understandable, and I don=E2=80=99t think I will have any prob=
lems
being late with packing in the future, but it was a pretty wild explosion
to witness. We were saying sorry for like 10 minutes straight lol.

Martinson=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and I made it safely to Okayama to spend the ni=
ght, and I spent
the last 15 minutes of the day doing all of the dirty dishes in the
apartment. I never got told thank you or anything but it felt great to do
something to help someone even if it may have gone unnoticed. I think that
we can learn a lot from =E2=80=9Cunsolicited service=E2=80=9D. I will try a=
nd write a
spiritual message about that below. Anyways, I went to bed afterwards, and
it may have been an even worse sleep than the last time I slept over there.
I was super cold all night, and I tried desperately to cover myself with a
towel as I slept lol. I probably barely got any sleep, but I lived to tell
the tale fortunately.

Or unfortunately=E2=80=A6
Saturday morning I had to throw my towel and guitar back in my bags and
book It for the station, I had no idea I needed to leave early so I was
super Stressed. On the way to the station, because I was carrying a full
suitcase, carry on and backpack, the 3 Elders in front of me Left me in the
dust and took the train we needed to ride before I could catch up. That
left me alone without a sim card to try and travel 3=C2=BD hours to Osaka.
Fortunately, I did somehow manage to make it all by myself, but having not
eaten anything all morning I was on the brink of passing out from lugging
around so much alone. It was brutal.

Sunday-Monday
Since arriving in Sennan, I have done some much needed vacuuming, traveled
to stake conference, and enjoyed Listening to reports as my companion is
the district Leader. Cool story, I made a Jimoty post on Saturday evening,
and Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 didn't have high hopes to say the least. Appa=
rently he had
previously made a post for a game night and nobody was interested. Anyways,
we checked on the post the next day, and there were already 4 people
interested in being our friends =F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=98=B1=F0=9F=
=99=8C=F0=9F=99=8C Huge blessing, let's just hope
they respond quickly and positively! JIMOTY LETS GO
I also managed to find a speaker for my guitar on Pday, but when I brought
it home to try out, it worked for a few minutes and then smoke started
coming out of it. Now it only makes a buzzing sound that will likely
produce more smoke if I leave it turned on. Hey, if I need to set off a
fire alarm I am SET =F0=9F=94=A5=F0=9F=94=A5 I am pretty bummed and frustra=
ted though, maybe I
will just save up my personal money for a few weeks and try to find a nicer
speaker or something, bummer.

Spiritual Thought Time!
I mentioned I wanted to talk a little about =E2=80=9Cunsolicited service,=
=E2=80=9D so I
will try to come up with something =F0=9F=A7=A0=F0=9F=94=8C
In our lives, we spend a lot of time doing things that benefit ourselves.
This isn't necessarily a bad thing, it's absolutely important to take care
of ourselves, but I have noticed something by paying less attention to my
own wants. As I focus my energy towards fulfilling God's will and
strengthening those around me, I find that my heart is more full, and my
conscience is less troubled by my worries and concerns. I am by no means
perfect at this, but I'd encourage whoever is reading this to spend some
time in which you'd regularly indulge in personal wants or activities and
do something for one of your friends or family members. They don't even
have to be someone you know! If you make some time for others without the
sole intention of praise or reward, you will feel spiritually full. I
believe that this is true, I have experienced it firsthand!

I love you guys, I hope you are doing ok in your lives. I can't wait to
message/hear from you all. hang In there!

=E3=82=AD=E3=83=AA=E3=82=A2=E3=83=B3=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81

